CMEPS: ESMF trace regions for the mediator restart write path (diagnostic only)

APPLIES ON TOP OF cmeps-mediator-restart-io.patch.

Purely additive. No existing line is modified or removed; the only new code is
ESMF_TraceRegionEnter/Exit calls, and use statements for those Trace Regions, and
comments, so it cannot change results. The regions nest under the existing
MED:(med_phases_restart_write) entry in ESMF_Profile.summary -- no new output
files, no tooling, no namelist.

Why: med_phases_restart_write is 288-336 s of an ACCESS-OM3 8 km 1-day run,
34-39% of the wall clock, with 6697 of 8216 PETs idle through it, and it is one
opaque block -- med_io_mod has no timers at all.

Watching the restart file grow shows it arriving in bursts of a few GB separated
by pauses of tens of seconds: roughly one cycle per FieldBundle (25.26 GB in ~14
bundles, 1.80 GB and ~24 s each). That points at a per-bundle cost that moves no
file bytes, and two candidates sit exactly there -- pio_initdecomp, which builds
the rearranger schedule collectively once per FieldBundle, and the unconditional
ESMF_LogWrite of the dof array beside it. Neither has ever been timed.

What you get:

  med_io_wopen             1                file create/open
  med_io_FB_defvar         per whead call   variable definitions
  med_io_enddef            1                pio_enddef
  med_io_FB_dof            per wdata call   distgrid query + per-bundle LogWrite
  med_io_FB_initdecomp     per wdata call   pio_initdecomp -- no file I/O
  med_io_FB_darray         per wdata call   pio_write_darray loop -- the bytes
  med_io_FB_coords         per wdata call   coordinate writes, if enabled
  med_io_FB_freedecomp     per wdata call   pio_freedecomp
  med_io_close             1                pio_closefile -- under netcdf4p this is
                                            where HDF5 finally flushes, so a large
                                            cost here is the write landing, not a
                                            close

How to read it:

  med_io_FB_initdecomp large -> the pauses are the decomposition build, and the
      cache dropped from this patch series is the fix
  med_io_FB_darray ~= all of it -> the write really is bandwidth bound and fewer
      bytes is the only lever
  med_io_close large -> the per-bundle picture is wrong and the cost is one
      deferred flush at the end
  med_io_FB_dof large -> it is the per-bundle ESMF_LogWrite, which is a one-line
      fix

Those are three different fixes. Do not write any of them before the numbers say
which.

Caveat: med_io_FB_defvar, med_io_FB_dof, med_io_FB_darray and med_io_wopen span
blocks containing if (ChkErr(...)) return, so on an error path they exit without
closing and that run's profile is unbalanced. med_io_FB_initdecomp,
med_io_FB_coords, med_io_FB_freedecomp, med_io_enddef and med_io_close are
enter/call/exit with no return in between. An error aborts the run anyway.

Touches mediator/med_io_mod.F90 only.

